.TH ZDOTS-HYGIENE 1 "2026-08-12" "zdots" "zdots manual"
.SH NAME
zdots-hygiene \- zdots\-hygiene — Unified system storage hygiene & eviction routine
.SH SYNOPSIS
See OPTIONS below (generated from \fBzdots-hygiene --help\fR).
.SH OPTIONS
.nf
zdots-hygiene — Unified system storage hygiene & eviction routine

Usage:
  zdots-hygiene [options]

Options:
  (no flag)     Dry run mode — preview reclaimable space and actions
  -f, --apply   Execute non-destructive cleanup sweeps
  -h, --help    Show this help message

Actions Executed on --apply:
  1. Docker/Colima VM: Prune unused images/volumes & run fstrim inside Colima
  2. Python uv Cache: Clear package/build caches (uv cache clean)
  3. Homebrew: Remove old formula bottles & clear brew download cache
  4. Ingestion Buffer: Evict staged media/docs in ingest-sources > 7 days old
  5. Diagnostic Logs: Remove stale trace dumps (collector-diag-*.jsonl) > 14 days old
  6. Agent Runtimes: Purge obsolete codex-runtimes cache
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
agent-guide(1), zdots-doctor(1)
